  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA-only, multi-profile, PCA n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, substantially outperforming single-profile RNA (0.485) and image-only (0.208). Within multi-profile, avgpool (0.591) clearly beats transformer (0.519), establishing avgpool as the preferred aggregation. Uncertainty: we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA n2000). Whether a learned representation (scvi_n200) can outperform a linear one is an open and important question. This experiment (config_005: scvi_n200, multi-profile, avgpool) changes only the RNA encoder relative to config_002, cleanly isolating the effect of representation quality while holding the best-known profile and aggregation settings fixed. If scvi_n200 improves, it signals that encoder choice is a high-leverage axis worth further exploration (e.g., scgpt); if it does not, PCA is likely sufficient and budget is better spent investigating multimodal fusion or other axes. Under a limited budget, this single-variable comparison maximizes information gained per experiment."
